CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer vzalloc(sizeof(*pstapriv->pallocated_stainfo_buf)...) over vzalloc(sizeof(struct sta_info)...)
#44: FILE: drivers/staging/rtl8188eu/core/rtw_sta_mgt.c:71:
+	pstapriv->pallocated_stainfo_buf = vzalloc(sizeof(struct sta_info) *

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

